<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <dimen name="collapsed_cover_size">64dp</dimen>
    <!-- Corner radius for feed card art (rounded_rectangle_cover) and history thumbnails (CardView),
         both via ?itemCorner. Phone default; bumped to 12dp on TV in values-land-television/dimens.xml. -->
    <dimen name="item_corner">8dp</dimen>
    <!-- Width reserved at the trailing edge of the collapsed mini-player for the play/pause control
         (48dp button + 8dp padding each side). Referenced by BOTH item_player_collapsed_controls.xml
         (the live bar) and item_player_collapsed.xml (the invisible twin measured for the collapse
         animation): the two title columns must reserve the identical end width, or the title shifts
         horizontally as the player collapses. Single source of truth so they can't drift. -->
    <dimen name="collapsed_end_controls_width">64dp</dimen>

    <!-- Ceiling for the full-screen player's metadata pill (trackSubtitle). 210dp = the measured 185dp of
         "MPEG - 44100 Hz - 2ch - 320 kbps" in Roboto at 12sp plus its 10dp horizontal padding each side.
         Deliberately has NO values-land override: landscape is short, not narrow - its controls column is
         a weighted half of ~914dp, comparable to portrait's 411dp - so a second value would only create
         the drift risk documented on collapsed_end_controls_width without buying anything. -->
    <dimen name="player_pill_max_width">210dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="context_menu_cover_size">48dp</dimen>
    <!-- Ceiling on the full-screen player's square cover (BasePlayerTrackCoverContainer sets both
         layout_constraintWidth_max and layout_constraintHeight_max to this, with dimensionRatio 1,1).
         384dp → 448dp on 2026-09-09. THE REASON IS DENSITY, NOT DEVICE.

         WHAT WAS WRONG. The cover is width-bound, never height-bound, so it takes screenWidth minus its
         32dp of margins — UNTIL this cap binds, after which extra screen room becomes dead space instead
         of cover. The cap binds when screenWidthDp - 32 > cap, i.e. above 416dp of width. A Pixel 10 is
         1080px wide, so it is 411dp at the factory density of 420 and 485dp at 356 (Display size set to
         its smallest). FACTORY DENSITY CLEARS THE OLD CAP BY 1.1% AND NOTHING ELSE DOES:
           420: available 379dp → cover 379dp = 92% of the screen.
           356: available 453dp → cover CAPPED at 384dp = 79%, with the difference pooling as slack at
                both ends of the packed chain (measured on device: player_track_cover 854x854 px, which is
                384dp to the pixel).
         Any user who reduces Display size, and any phone wider than 416dp, got the 79% layout.

         ⚠️ 420 CANNOT CHANGE, BY CONSTRUCTION — THIS IS THE PROOF, NOT AN OBSERVATION. Available width at
         420 is 379dp, which is already below the OLD cap; the cover is limited by its margins there, not
         by this value. So ANY cap >= 380dp leaves factory density bit-identical. 448 is chosen to land 356
         at 448/485 = 92.4%, matching 420's 92.2% rather than exceeding it, while keeping a real ceiling for
         tablets (at 800dp wide: 48% → 56%).

         ⚠️ LANDSCAPE IS AFFECTED AND THAT WAS CHECKED, NOT ASSUMED — DO NOT RE-RAISE IT. This dimen sits
         on BasePlayerTrackCoverContainer, the parent of BOTH the portrait style and the values-land one,
         and the cap already binds in landscape today. Measured and reconciled:
           today, 420, landscape:    cover 384dp = 1008px in a 1080px-tall screen → ~36px clearance,
                                     and that is what the app ships with and looks correct on device.
           proposed, 356, landscape: cover 448dp =  997px → ~42px clearance, i.e. MORE room than the
                                     default configuration already runs with.
         Raising the cap moves landscape TOWARD a clearance the app already ships, not away from one. No
         values-land override, no split value, no new mechanism — deliberately, because a second value
         would create exactly the drift risk documented on collapsed_end_controls_width.
         PRECEDENT FOR CHECKING RATHER THAN ASSUMING: an earlier session caught "Landscape risk — 388dp
         AppBarLayout would fill entire screen in landscape (no layout-land variant exists)" before
         building. Same shape of risk, same answer: measure the landscape configuration first.
         layout-land/fragment_player.xml is a maintained surface, edited in at least two prior sessions.

         PROVENANCE, BECAUSE AN UNEXPLAINED CONSTANT DESERVES IT: this is inherited upstream scaffolding.
         `git log -S max_cover_size` puts it in 3817ceb5 "Initial Commit, Only contains base UI" at 280dp,
         later raised to 384dp — with NO COMMENT IN ANY REVISION. Both readings belong here: a constant
         whose reason is unrecorded warrants caution, AND it has already been raised once with no recorded
         fallout, which is evidence it is tunable rather than load-bearing.

         RESIDUAL SLACK IS NOT FIXED BY THIS AND IS NOT MEANT TO BE. Growing the cover adds 64dp to the
         packed chain, so the leftover pooled at each end drops by roughly a third — it does not vanish.
         That is structural: paddingTop/paddingBottom on PlayerExpandedConstraintLayout are RESERVATIONS
         (expanded toolbar, more-sheet peek), not spacing knobs. THE NAMED LEVER IS THE CHAIN BIAS — see
         PlayerTrackCoverContainer in styles.xml, "Neither is a spacing knob; the cover chain's bias is."
         CONSIDERED AND NOT TAKEN 2026-09-09: bias changes 420, which is the one configuration that must
         not move, and the cover proportion was the complaint rather than the slack. -->
    <dimen name="max_cover_size">448dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="media_header_cover_size">250dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="bottom_player_peek_height">136dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="nav_width">@dimen/collapsed_cover_size</dimen>
    <dimen name="nav_height">@dimen/collapsed_cover_size</dimen>
    <dimen name="player_info_peek_height">@dimen/nav_height</dimen>
    <dimen name="player_more_top_margin">78dp</dimen>

    <!-- Fixed heights for the nested horizontal RecyclerView in HorizontalListViewHolder,
         per Shelf.Lists subtype, so the row doesn't visually collapse-then-expand while its
         adapter is still populating. Estimated from each item layout's content; tune visually
         if a type looks clipped or has excess empty space. -->
    <dimen name="shelf_media_text_block_height_radio">45dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="shelf_category_row_height">68dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="shelf_three_tracks_row_height">216dp</dimen>

    <!-- Backing dimens for the ?itemCoverSize theme attr (see themes.xml) and the section-header text size,
         so both can be TV-overridden in values-land-television/. These phone values equal the previous
         inline literals, so phone/tablet render identically. -->
    <dimen name="item_cover_size">96dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="item_cover_size_big">128dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="shelf_header_text_size">20sp</dimen>
</resources>